# the ELF image writer: an executable from the image record of a link
#
# every address, file offset and size comes from the layout record, and every
# byte of an output section from the relocated record, so the writer computes
# no address. it builds the ELF model the ELF writer turns into bytes. the
# header takes its machine, class and byte order from the architecture row,
# its e_flags, EI_OSABI and EI_ABIVERSION from the settled facts and traits,
# and its entry from the entry symbol. a PT_LOAD maps each segment of the
# layout, PT_TLS the thread-local block, PT_NOTE each run of loaded notes,
# PT_GNU_PROPERTY the GNU property note and PT_GNU_STACK the stack, which is
# executable only when an input's stack note asks for it. the section headers
# list the output sections in image order, then the symbol table and the
# string tables. a link that needs what the image cannot hold yet is refused,
# naming what it needs.
#
# the GNU property note is a table the linker makes: its declarer sizes it
# from the settled facts and traits before layout, and the writer fills the
# place layout gave it with the same bytes.

